# The judge profile of trajectory transforms: the model `ask` and transforms/atlas.py call (prl/algo/llm_client.py),
# sourced by ota_transform.env and ota_atlas_judge.env; not an arm by itself. Any OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions
# endpoint. Set the endpoint, model and key file in your site profile (configs/sites/<site>.env) or the environment;
# the values here are only the defaults. The key is a private file (0600), never in the environment or the repo.
PRL_JUDGE_API_BASE=${PRL_JUDGE_API_BASE:-}       # e.g. https://<provider>/v1
PRL_JUDGE_MODEL=${PRL_JUDGE_MODEL:-}
PRL_JUDGE_KEY_FILE=${PRL_JUDGE_KEY_FILE:-$PRL_EXT/private/judge_api_key}
PRL_JUDGE_PROMPT=${PRL_JUDGE_PROMPT:-paper}
# A JSON object sent with every request, e.g. '{"reasoning_effort": "medium"}'. Set it explicitly, so that a change of
# the provider's default cannot change the judge in the middle of a run.
PRL_JUDGE_EXTRA_BODY=${PRL_JUDGE_EXTRA_BODY:-}
# Requests in flight; a 429 waits without using an attempt (llm_client.RATE_LIMIT_WAIT). At 16, rewriting every trial
# of a 32 x 8 rollout took 32-44 min per rollout, most of it in the teacher's queue.
PRL_JUDGE_CONCURRENCY=${PRL_JUDGE_CONCURRENCY:-32}
# Models asked in turn when the one before refuses a prompt (a provider's content filter); empty: one model only.
PRL_JUDGE_FALLBACK_MODELS=${PRL_JUDGE_FALLBACK_MODELS-}
